  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader far down a long page, I want the page to come back where I was when iOS killed the web content process in the background, so that I do not land back on the flag message or at the top.\n\n### Scenario\nRead far down a long page, background the app, iOS kills the WebContent process. On return the same document reloads and lands on `document.anchor` (the original flag message), or at the top without an anchor. With tap-to-load on, images already tapped are placeholders again.\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderWebController.swift:283-294` (`contentProcessTerminated`): a ready document is loaded again with `loadPage(document)`, nothing saved.\n- Same file `:251-256`: at ready, the landing is `document.anchor`, else `savedReadingTop`; `savedReadingTop` is set only in `show()` (`:144`).\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Viewer/ReaderWebController+Viewer.swift:16-22`: `decisions(for:)` builds `ImageDecision` without `tapped:`.\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/.../ReaderInsetsWebTests.swift:71-85` pins the reload-once rule only.\n\n### Fix\nKeep the last `.position(post:)` the page reported for the shown document (it already passes through `handle`) and land on it after a termination reload; pass `tapped: consented.contains(text)` in `decisions(for:)`.\n\n### Tests (fail before the fix)\n`ReaderWebControllerTests.aReloadAfterProcessTerminationLandsOnTheLastReportedPost` (hosted: document with anchor A, report `.position(post: B)`, call `webViewWebContentProcessDidTerminate`, wait for ready, the topmost article is B); a second test: a tapped third-party image is loaded after the reload.\n\nRework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
